  "reason": "The records collectively connect temperature-dependent mechanical response in HEAs with dislocation activity, lattice distortion, stacking faults/FCC–HCP behavior, and high-temperature softening. R5 additionally supplies elevated-temperature tribology of an HEA film, while R6, R10, and R17 show degradation or changes in strength and elastic response at high temperature. However, none describes the specific FeNiCrCoCu-on-Cu coating, combined nanoindentation/friction molecular-dynamics protocol, or the reported transition near 900 K from stacking-fault-mediated deformation to lattice disorder with simultaneous dislocation-density reduction and increased friction. Thus the literature points in the right direction but leaves the particular intervention and integrated mechanism as a substantial new step."
